 "notes": "Single 18-hole course (no multiple nines) - facility has one course only, Golf Canada course id 21066 / facility 20962. Six tee sets: Black, Blue, Blue/White (combo), White, Green, Red. 'rating'/'slope' are the men's course/slope ratings printed on the card and held by Golf Canada; 'ratingWomen'/'slopeWomen' are Golf Canada's women's ratings for the same tees (no women's rating exists for Black or Blue). The card prints two stroke-index rows: Men's HDCP (stored as 'handicap') and Ladies' HDCP (stored as 'handicapWomen'). DISCREPANCY: Golf Canada's per-hole yardages for the GREEN tee are wrong - they duplicate the White tee on 17 of 18 holes and total 5868. The operator's printed card and mScorecard both give Green as 2742/2701 = 5443, which is also consistent with Golf Canada's own Green rating of 65.9/112. Green 5443 is used here. DISCREPANCY: the official PDF contains a hidden older text layer (and several aggregators, e.g. GolfLink, still publish it) with a longer, differently-rated card: Black 7240 (76.1/140), Blue 6576 (72.5/133), Blue/White 6282 (70.6/127), White 6010 (69.0/124), Green 5478 (66.6/119), Red 5092 (69.2/120). That set is superseded - it is not what renders on the current card and does not match Golf Canada. Yardages are measured to the centre of the green. Hole 8 is a long par 3 (274 from Black) and hole 7 is a par 4 of 494 from Black."
